Suggested approach for Build a validated form workflow:
1. Implement the requirement in the named App Router convention or trusted server layer.
2. Add explicit input validation and a user-friendly empty/error/denied state.
3. Exercise the normal case and at least one boundary case.
4. Run lint/tests and a production build in the target Next.js version.

Starter to adapt:
'use server';
import { revalidatePath } from 'next/cache';
export async function addNote(formData) { const title = String(formData.get('title') || '').trim(); if (!title) return { error: 'Required' }; revalidatePath('/notes'); return { success: true }; }

Required static markers: use server, revalidatePath, formData.get. These only provide a limited automatic signal; acceptance criteria must be manually reviewed.
